    <entry>
        <title>Malfunctioning</title>
        <author>
            <name>AdRoz78</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://adroz78.com/posts/malfunctioning/"/>
        <id>https://adroz78.com/posts/malfunctioning/</id>
            <category term="my_art"/>
            <category term="AIC-RF/2"/>

        <updated>2026-10-24T23:01:00+02:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                    <div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="1" data-is-empty="false">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://adroz78.com/media/posts/10/gallery/malfunctioning-new.png" data-size="3360x1440"><img loading="lazy" src="https://adroz78.com/media/posts/10/gallery/malfunctioning-new-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="329"></a></figure>
</div></div>
<p>Once about every 30 minutes AIC starts to glitch out like in the photo. This glitching can be compared to something of a mix between a stroke and lobotomy, with him knowing that he is malfunctioning but not being able to do anything about it. After at most 30 seconds, though, his system realizes that something's up and restarts the AI, restoring him back to normal.</p>

                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                <div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="1" data-is-empty="false">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://adroz78.com/media/posts/10/gallery/malfunctioning-new.png" data-size="3360x1440"><img loading="lazy" src="https://adroz78.com/media/posts/10/gallery/malfunctioning-new-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="329"></a></figure>
</div></div>
<p>Once about every 30 minutes AIC starts to glitch out like in the photo. This glitching can be compared to something of a mix between a stroke and lobotomy, with him knowing that he is malfunctioning but not being able to do anything about it. After at most 30 seconds, though, his system realizes that something's up and restarts the AI, restoring him back to normal.</p>

<p>As for the scene shown, don't worry, by the time the other character came out of the initial shock he was only able to shoot once before AIC stopped glitching, atfer which, well.. this is a General submission, use your imaginaton to finish it. Though for those who'd like to see something more mature I do have an artwork planned.<br><br>This artwork took ages to do, and while I was doing it I both got sick twice, and lost my Ibis Paint data (thankfully not the artwork files themselves, but everything else yeah, including brushes =[ ). I feel like I outdid myself again, though I originally drew this with making a wallpaper in mind.<br><br>If for whatever reason you want this as your wallpaper contact me through any of my linked socials and I will send the full resolution version (2K). Still with watermarks though =].<br><br>Have a good day and don't give up!</p>
            ]]>
        </content>
    </entry>
